    An arc is a curve, so it encloses nothing and has no area. It is held as a centre, a radius, the angle it
    starts at and the angle it sweeps through, signed: positive sweeps counter-clockwise and negative clockwise.
    A sweep of a whole turn is allowed and draws the full circle; a sweep of nothing is not, because an arc that
    goes nowhere has no direction and no length.

    How far an arc is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where an arc crosses another shape.

