class GeoCircle3(System.ValueType):
    """Whether a circle touches another shape.

    Represents a circular disc in 3D space, defined by a centre, a normal and a radius.

    Like a polygon, this is a planar region rather than a curve: it has an area, and a point counts as inside it
    only when the point lies on the carrier plane as well as within the radius.

    How far a circle is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a circle crosses another shape.

    The point of a circle nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it faces
    one.

    A circle asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, where they cross, and where the
    shortest segment between them runs.

    A circle asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest
    segment between them runs.

    A circle asked whether its rim touches an infinite line and where they cross."""
