class GeoFace3(System.Object):
    """Whether a face touches another shape.

    Represents a flat face in 3D space: an outer boundary polygon with optional holes cut out of it.

    A face is what a polygon becomes once it needs to carry openings. A plate with bolt holes, a wall with a
    window: the outer loop says where the material ends and each inner loop says where it is missing. Every loop
    shares one plane, which is checked at construction.

    How far a face is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a face crosses another shape.

    What a face in space can answer by working in its own plane: combining it with another flat shape lying in
    that same plane.

    The point of a face nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it faces
    one.

    A face asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, where they cross, and where the
    shortest segment between them runs.

    A face asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest segment
    between them runs.

    A face asked about an infinite line: whether they touch, how far apart they are, where they cross and where
    the shortest segment between them runs."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, boundary: GeoPolygon3) -> None:
