class GeoObb3(System.Object):
    """Whether an oriented box touches another shape.

    Represents an oriented bounding box (OBB): a cuboid that carries its own orientation rather than lining up
    with the world axes.

    This is a shape, not a bound. A beam running at an angle is described tightly by an oriented box and only
    loosely by an axis-aligned one, which is what GeoAabb3 is for. The price is that testing two oriented boxes
    against each other needs the separating axis theorem rather than six comparisons, so the usual pattern is to
    reject with bounding boxes first and reach for this only on what survives.

    How far an oriented box is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where an oriented box crosses another shape.

    The point of an oriented box nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of
    it faces one.

    An oriented box asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, and where the shortest
    segment between them runs.

    A box asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest segment
    between them runs.

    An oriented box asked whether it touches an infinite line, how far apart they are and where they cross."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, coordinateSystem: GeoCoordinateSystem3, sizeX: float, sizeY: float, sizeZ: float) -> None:
        """Initializes a box from a local coordinate system and its sizes."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, center: GeoPoint3, sizeX: float, sizeY: float, sizeZ: float) -> None:
        """Initializes a box aligned with the world axes."""
    @overload
    def __init__(
