class GeoPlane3(System.ValueType):
    """Whether a plane touches another shape.

    Represents an infinite 3D plane defined by a point on the plane and a normal vector.

    The plane is oriented: it distinguishes the side its normal points towards from the other side. That is what
    lets GeoPlane3.SignedDistanceTo and GeoPlane3.GetSide answer at all, and it is why GeoPlane3.Flip is a
    meaningful operation rather than a no-op.

    How far a plane is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a plane crosses another shape.

    The point of a plane nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it faces
    one.

    A plane asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, and where the shortest segment
    between them runs.

    A plane asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest
    segment between them runs.

    A plane asked about an infinite line: whether they touch, how far apart they are, where they cross and where
    the shortest segment between them runs; and the line two planes share."""
