class GeoPolygon2(System.Object):
    """Whether a polygon touches another shape.

    Represents a 2D closed polygon.

    A polygon is expected to be simple — no edge crossing another — but this is not checked, because checking
    costs more than every other thing the constructor does put together. A polygon whose edges do cross is still
    usable rather than undefined: containment reads it under the even-odd rule, so a region enclosed an even
    number of times counts as outside, and every operation built on containment follows suit. What does not
    survive is area. GeoPolygon2.SignedArea sums lobes with their own signs, so a figure-eight reports zero
    however large its lobes are, and GeoPolygon2.Area reports zero with it.

    How far a polygon is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a polygon crosses another shape.

    The point of a polygon nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it
    faces one.

    A polygon asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest
    segment between them runs."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, vertices: Sequence[GeoPoint2] | System.Array[GeoPoint2]) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polygon directly from parameter vertices."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, *vertices: GeoPoint2) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polygon directly from parameter vertices."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, vertices: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[GeoPoint2]) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polygon from a list of vertices. Duplicate vertex at the end to close the loop will be
        automatically removed."""
