class GeoPolyline3(System.Object):
    """Whether a polyline touches another shape.

    Represents an open polygonal chain of 3D points.

    A polyline is always an open chain: it never joins its last vertex back to its first, and it encloses
    nothing. Geometry meant to enclose an area is a GeoPolygon3, and GeoPolyline3.ToPolygon converts between
    them. That is why a polyline offers IsPointOn but no Contains: a curve has no interior for a point to be
    inside of.

    The vertices need not be coplanar. A polyline may wander freely through space, which is what separates it
    from a polygon and is why it carries no normal and no area.

    How far a polyline is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a polyline crosses another shape.

    The point of a polyline nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it
    faces one.

    A polyline asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, where they cross, and where the
    shortest segment between them runs.

    A polyline asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest
    segment between them runs.

    A polyline asked about an infinite line: whether they touch, how far apart they are, where they cross and
    where the shortest segment between them runs."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, vertices: Sequence[GeoPoint3] | System.Array[GeoPoint3]) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polyline directly from vertex arguments."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, *vertices: GeoPoint3) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polyline directly from vertex arguments."""
    @overload
    def __init__(self, vertices: System.Collections.Generic.IEnumerable[GeoPoint3]) -> None:
        """Initializes a new polyline from a sequence of vertices."""
    @property
    def EdgeCount(self) -> int:
        """Gets the number of segments, one fewer than the number of vertices."""
    @property
    def EndPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the last vertex, where the chain ends."""
    @property
    def Length(self) -> float:
        """Gets the total length of the polyline."""
    @property
    def MidPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the point half way along the chain."""
    @property
    def StartPoint(self) -> GeoPoint3:
        """Gets the first vertex, where the chain starts."""
    @property
    def VertexCount(self) -> int:
        """Gets the number of vertices."""
    @property
