class GeoSolid3(System.Object):
    """Whether a solid touches another shape.

    Represents a 3D solid body as the set of faces bounding it, with optional openings carved out.

    The faces are expected to be wound so their normals point out of the body, and to close it without gaps.
    Neither is enforced, because checking costs a full pass over every edge and most solids come from a modeller
    that already guarantees it; GeoSolid3.IsClosed is there for the ones that do not. What the guarantees buy is
    GeoSolid3.GetVolume and GeoSolid3.Contains: both read the body as a filled region and neither means anything
    for a shell with a hole in it.

    An opening is a whole solid subtracted from this one — a duct through a slab, a recess in a footing. It is
    not the same thing as a hole in a GeoFace3, which is flat and belongs to a single face.

    How far a solid is from another shape, and how deep inside one it sits.

    Where a solid crosses another shape.

    The point of a solid nearest another shape, the shortest segment joining the two, and which edge of it faces
    one.

    A solid asked about a ball: how far apart they are, whether they touch, and where the shortest segment
    between them runs.

    A solid asked how far it is from a spline, whether they touch, where they cross and where the shortest
    segment between them runs.

    A solid asked about an infinite line: whether they touch, how far apart they are, where the line crosses its
    surface and where the shortest segment between them runs."""
